        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Or course:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    b = { input = { '%b()', '^.().*().$' }, output = { left = '(', right = ')' } },\r\n    B = { input = { '%b{}', '^.().*().$' }, output = { left = '{', right = '}' } },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, this is also possible with `sr)}` which is pretty similar from ergonomic point of view. The [built-in `b` surrounding](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4228f166ee9db3e910eea1915e2d3683028add47/doc/mini-surround.txt#L175-L176) is pretty useful by itself.",
